35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems that sitting close to one another helps us learn and collaborate much more naturally than we realize.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The current plan is unfair; some get windows while others don't. Also, unplanned shuffles are incredibly disruptive to our productivity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found out that we are billed by area, not people... and moving the power lines costs money every single time we change.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,Oh no! The pilot floor takes almost ten minutes just to start working! And those shuffles sound like a total nightmare.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. The noise is uneven across the room, and adjusting the equipment to fit your body takes days. Constant moving is a disaster.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Daisuke, thank you for checking the costs. If moving is expensive and disruptive, perhaps we should be very careful with our choice.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, if the equipment takes days to settle, then a fixed position is logically superior for physical health and focus.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just don't want us to waste the budget. If we change the layout too often, the costs will just keep adding up.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"But if we stay in one spot, do we lose that ""spark"" Shizue mentioned? I don't want us to become silos!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"A ""spark"" isn't worth a backache or a headache from the printer noise. We need stability and a proper setup.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"Perhaps there is a way to have both? Stability for the body, but a way to ensure we still talk to each other.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The window issue is the most pressing point of inequality. We cannot simply let a few people have all the light.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If we go with something that changes often, the facilities quotes say we'll pay every time. That seems... risky.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"Wait, if we have to plug in every morning, that's so much wasted time! I can't handle that in my schedule.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Then we are all agreeing that ""Free Address"" is a terrible idea. It's expensive, noisy, and physically draining.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Let us look at the other options with these worries in mind.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,We must decide how to handle the inequality of the desks. Rotating them might be the only fair solution.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm worried about the cost of rotating... would that count as a ""change to the plan"" for the wiring?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mio,,I just want something that doesn't take forever to set up and doesn't involve half-packed boxes for two weeks!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's see the options. I suspect I'll be voting for whatever keeps me in one quiet, adjusted chair.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
